Target pool:
: <?=sel("cache_pool", $pcsettings_cache_pool, $pool_options);?> <span style="display:block;margin-top:2px;">The pool selected here must also be the share's <b>Primary storage</b></span>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p>Pool the media is copied to. One pool only.</p>
        <p>The list shows real pools only: unRAID pools and ZFS pools.</p>
        <p>Important: The pool selected here must also be the share's <b>Primary storage</b>. If the share still points at the array, or <b>Primary storage</b> is set to another pool, the plugin will not work as intended and the disks <b>will spin up</b>.</p>
</blockquote>

Cache Copy Mode:
: <?=sel("copy_scope", $pcsettings_copy_scope, array("" => "Files in use", "folder" => "Always the whole folder"), ' id="copy_scope" onchange="showCopyHint()"');?> <span id="copy_hint" style="display:block;margin-top:2px;"></span>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p><b>Files in use:</b> for a movie, the playing file plus the subtitles and nfo next to it, nothing from subfolders. For a series episode, the season folder, as set under "Skip earlier episodes".</p>
        <p><b>Always the whole folder:</b> everything in the playing file's folder, subfolders included, for movies and series alike.</p>
        <p>Folders listed under "Never cache these" are always left out, in both modes.</p>
