Skip earlier episodes:
: <?=sel("skip_earlier_episodes", $pcsettings_skip_earlier_episodes == "on" ? "on" : "off", array("off" => "Off", "on" => "On"));?>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p><b>On:</b> When an episode plays, only that episode and the episodes after it in the season folder are copied, in file name order, plus all subtitles, nfo and artwork. Earlier episodes stay on the array. Jumping back to an earlier episode caches from there on at the next copy run.</p>
        <p><b>Off:</b> The whole season folder is copied, subfolders included.</p>
</blockquote>

Open file handles:
: <?php if ($gdb_status == "ok") { echo '<span style="white-space:nowrap;">Will switch to the cache copy while playback continues, <b class="green" style="display:inline !important;">gdb is available</b></span>'; } elseif ($gdb_status == "nopython") { echo 'Switching needs gdb but <b class="red" style="display:inline !important;">gdb cannot find python3</b>, re-run the plugin install, it installs both, the plugin still copies and leaves the open handles on the array'; } elseif ($gdb_status == "broken") { echo 'Switching needs gdb but <b class="red" style="display:inline !important;">gdb does not run</b> (' . htmlspecialchars(substr($gdb_out, 0, 90)) . '), the plugin still copies and leaves the open handles on the array'; } else { echo 'Switching needs gdb but <b class="red" style="display:inline !important;">gdb was not found</b>, re-run the plugin install, the plugin still copies and leaves the open handles on the array'; } ?>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p>Once the copy is complete the open handle moves from the array to the cache copy, so the array disk can spin down while you keep watching. This needs the gdb package, which the plugin installs. gdb itself uses python3, so the plugin installs that too when it is missing. Without gdb the plugin logs it and leaves the handle where it is.</p>
</blockquote>

