<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-hand-peace-o title"></i>Logging and Notifications</span></div>

syslog:
: <?=sel("log_to_syslog", $pcsettings_log_to_syslog == "yes" ? "yes" : "no", array("yes" => "yes", "no" => "no"));?>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p>"yes" also sends the event lines to syslog, so they show up in the unRAID system log: real work like files cached and handles switched, plus errors and warnings. A scheduled run that does nothing logs nothing.</p>
        <p>The plugin always writes its own log file, the Log tab reads that one. Manual runs tell the whole story there, syslog only ever sees the events.</p>
</blockquote>

unRaid notifications:
: <?=sel("notifications", $pcsettings_notifications == "yes" ? "yes" : "no", array("no" => "no", "yes" => "yes"));?>
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p>"yes" sends an Unraid notification when media is copied to the pool, and when a release removes cached copies.</p>
        <p>It also warns when a release keeps a file because it changed after it was copied: the pool and the array then hold different versions, check that pair. Errors are not notified, they are in the Log tab and, with syslog on, in the system log.</p>
</blockquote>

rsync copy command:
: <input type="text" name="rsync_command" maxlength="99" style="width:100%;" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($pcsettings_rsync_command, ENT_QUOTES);?>" placeholder="rsync -a --mkpath" >
<blockquote class='inline_help'>
        <p>The rsync command used to copy from array to cache. Default: "rsync -a --mkpath", --mkpath needs rsync 3.2.3 or newer.</p>
